<figure id="A5.T14" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 14: </span>
Odds ratio per interquartile range (<math id="A5.T14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math>) for each code-complexity
metric for the PredState task <span id="A5.T14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">with the
standard IMP semantics (K-semantics and SOS)</span>.
<math id="A5.T14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta(\Delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta(\Delta)</annotation></semantics></math> for a metric is the odds ratio for a correct
final-state prediction when that metric increases from its
<math id="A5.T14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{25}^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>25</mtext><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{25}^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> to its <math id="A5.T14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{75}^{\text{th}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext>75</mtext><mtext>th</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{75}^{\text{th}}</annotation></semantics></math> percentile, holding
other metrics fixed. Reported only for models with &lt;90% accuracy on
the PredState task
(Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ 4.1 Final-State Prediction (PredState) ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ PLSemanticsBench: Large Language Models as Programming Language Interpreters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) to mitigate class
imbalance. The largest absolute values in each row is shown in
boldface font.

</figcaption>
